    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38123" root="لوذ" body-key="l">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَوْذٌ</span></b>  The <i>side</i> of a mountain; and its <i>circuit:</i>
pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ألْوَاذٌ</span>. (S, A, L, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <i>A side,</i> or <i>lateral
part</i> or <i>tract,</i> of a country or region: (A:) and of
a thing; (TA;) as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَوْذَانٌ</span></b> : (K:) pl. as above.
(A.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <i>A place of bending</i> of a valley: pl. as
above. (L, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هُوَ بِلَوْذِ كَذَا</span>, and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَذَا</span> ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بِلَوْذَانِ</span></b> ,
<i>He,</i> or <i>it, is in the side of,</i> or <i>part adjacent to,
such a place</i> or <i>thing.</i> (L.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b5-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هُوَ لَوْذَهُ</span> <i>He is
near to him</i> or <i>it.</i> (L.)

